---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ProfileCard from '../components/ProfileCard.astro';
import { profile, badgeRows } from '../site.config';
---

<BaseLayout>
  <div class="home-grid">
    <ProfileCard />

    <div>
      <h1>{profile.name}</h1>

      <p class="role">
        <span>{profile.role}</span>
        {
          profile.roleLogo && (
            <img
              src={profile.roleLogo.src}
              alt={profile.roleLogo.alt}
              class="role-logo"
              width="100"
              height="100"
            />
          )
        }
      </p>

      <p class="focus muted">{profile.focus}</p>

      <div class="badges">
        {
          badgeRows.map((row) => (
            <div class="badge-row">
              <span class="badge-label">{row.label}</span>
              <span class="badge-items">
                {row.items.map((item) =>
                  item.href ? (
                    <a class="pill" href={item.href} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                      {item.logo && <img src={item.logo} alt="" />}
                      {item.label}
                    </a>
                  ) : (
                    <span class="pill">
                      {item.logo && <img src={item.logo} alt="" />}
                      {item.label}
                    </span>
                  )
                )}
              </span>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>

      <!-- ============================================================
           EDIT YOUR HOME PAGE TEXT BELOW.
           Add or remove <section class="section"> blocks freely.
           ============================================================ -->

      <section class="section">
        <h2>Who am I</h2>
        <p>
          I'm Joseph Alemu. I graduated from DePaul University in June 2026 with a bachelor's
          degree in computer science, and I'm now a master's student at the University of
          Chicago, studying computer science with a specialization in high-performance
          computing.
        </p>
        <p>
          My interests lie in HPC, GPU programming, low-latency engineering, and compilers. I
          also enjoy video game development and 3D modeling, which I've been doing for about
          six years now.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>Technical Journey</h2>
        <p>
          My journey started in my senior year of high school, where I took a course in digital
          electronics. That class had me building circuits on breadboards and soldering my own
          designs onto PCBs. One of my proudest achievements was a circuit that displayed a
          random number on an LCD display.
        </p>
        <p>
          I carried that interest in hardware with me into my first year as a computer science
          student at DePaul. Most of my first-year classes didn't hold my attention. Then I took
          Systems, and I learned an enormous amount from it: assembly, ROP exploits, system
          interrupts, caching, and a range of other compiler and OS concepts.
        </p>
        <p>
          That course turned out to be a pivotal moment, and the catalyst for pursuing research.
          Afterward I reached out to professors and landed a role as a systems research
          assistant at DePaul, where I learned a great deal about C++, the stages of a JIT
          compiler, and how large systems are built. Half a year in, I decided to explore other
          fields.
        </p>
        <p>
          That's what led me to Motorola Solutions. In 2025 I was accepted into the Motorola
          Solutions Foundation Scholarship program at DePaul, where I ran into problems I had
          never seen before — such as how to push millions of gene expressions through a long
          data pipeline without it taking weeks.
        </p>
        <p>
          Making progress on that work taught me the importance of maximizing the hardware you
          already have, and of heterogeneous computing. That's what led me to high-performance
          computing, where I am now.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>Hobbies</h2>
        <p>
          I love 3D modeling. I started when I was 16, and bought myself a drawing tablet six
          years ago as a reward for finishing a commission. I don't sculpt as much as I used to,
          but I still open ZBrush whenever a character idea gets hold of me.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>Contact me</h2>
        <p class="asks">
          Have an interesting project?<br />
          Got a job offer?<br />
          Have a question?<br />
          Want to talk?
        </p>
        <p><a href={`mailto:${profile.email}`}>{profile.email}</a></p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .role {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    font-size: 1.12rem;
    margin: 0.5rem 0 0;
    max-width: none;
  }

  .role-logo {
    height: 34px;
    width: auto;
    flex: none;
  }

  .focus {
    font-size: 1rem;
    margin: 0.1rem 0 1.1rem;
  }

  .badges {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .badge-row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem 0.7rem;
  }

  .badge-label {
    font-size: 1.02rem;
  }

  .badge-items {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.45rem;
  }

  .asks {
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }
</style>
